{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","roleHeading":"Article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Adding Undo to Your App","anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"1. Create the plugin","anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. Register and pass to Store","anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register the plugin with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for undo\/redo methods and "},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracking:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via "},{"code":"applyRestore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating "},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Wire platform UI","anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}]},{"code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the "},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" after each undoable dispatch."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Coalescing","anchor":"Coalescing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"coalescing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Undo and sync","anchor":"Undo-and-sync"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo is scoped to changes the local user made. If another device deletes an entity and the merge surfaces that mid-session, "},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" will not bring the row back, even though older undo snapshots still contain it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That has to be the rule, because the alternative is worse than a missing undo step: restoring the row records it as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"creation"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which syncs out and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed it was gone. One person’s undo would undo everybody’s delete."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks this in "},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID leaves the set the moment it becomes local again — the user creates it, or the row reappears on disk because the other device undid "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its"}]},{"type":"text","text":" delete — so nothing is permanently un-undoable. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" for the mechanics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps that don’t sync never hit this: nothing populates the set, and undo behaves exactly as it always has."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Memory","anchor":"Memory"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use "},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to bound memory for large state:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"kind":"article","title":"KeyValueStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"article","title":"Macros"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"kind":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin"}}}